{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674770",
      "title": "Introducing Resource Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 52,
      "videoOrder": 47,
      "sourceHash": "313fdfda03f804a9da90769e8f626c87d8976a82a6e2cd80b5d7dc65291c9e3d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.804,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "Now with pathless layout routes being added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 7.71,
          "en": "we got another important tool provided",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.71,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "by Remix with which we can work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 14.04,
          "en": "Now, there are a couple of other very useful tools though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.04,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "and one of those other useful tools are resource routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 21.415,
          "en": "Now, what's a resource route?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.415,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "At the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 26.46,
          "en": "all these routes load pages, when we click on a link",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.46,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "we see a page, and that is the most common use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 34.163,
          "en": "After all, we're building a website with Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.163,
          "end": 37.02,
          "en": "But sometimes you want to have certain links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.02,
          "end": 39.03,
          "en": "that load data instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.03,
          "end": 43.44,
          "en": "that yield data or a file or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.44,
          "end": 46.413,
          "en": "And Remix also supports this use case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.25,
          "end": 49.08,
          "en": "It's indeed exactly what we need here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.08,
          "end": 52.41,
          "en": "for the expenses.raw.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.41,
          "end": 55.569,
          "en": "Here, I actually don't wanna return a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.569,
          "end": 60.18,
          "en": "that should be displayed, but instead just some raw data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.18,
          "end": 63.891,
          "en": "And doing that is thankfully pretty straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.891,
          "end": 65.85,
          "en": "All you have to do is get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.85,
          "end": 70.85,
          "en": "of your component export and instead export a loader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.95,
          "end": 72.66,
          "en": "And we learned about loaders",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.66,
          "end": 74.583,
          "en": "in the Remix essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 78.48,
          "en": "Now, loaders are these functions which are called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.48,
          "end": 80.67,
          "en": "by Remix when you visit a page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.67,
          "end": 84.48,
          "en": "and then those functions load the data for the page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.48,
          "end": 86.73,
          "en": "and the page can then use that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.73,
          "end": 88.98,
          "en": "with help of useLoaderData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.98,
          "end": 91.74,
          "en": "That's what you learned in the essentials section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.74,
          "end": 93.33,
          "en": "and that's what we'll get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.33,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "to in the next course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "However, what's important to understand about loaders is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 101.34,
          "en": "that in the end, they are triggered when",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.34,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "a get request reaches a certain route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 106.14,
          "en": "And that is precisely what happens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.14,
          "end": 108.72,
          "en": "when you click a link, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.72,
          "end": 109.838,
          "en": "If I click on pricing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.838,
          "end": 113.19,
          "en": "a get request is sent to slash pricing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.19,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "And we can even see that in the developer tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 117.66,
          "en": "If we open the network tab there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.66,
          "end": 120.3,
          "en": "and reload the pricing page, we see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.3,
          "end": 123.603,
          "en": "that a get request was sent to slash pricing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 128.22,
          "en": "so that's what happens when we visit a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.22,
          "end": 131.16,
          "en": "And in the end, loaders are simply triggered whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.16,
          "end": 134.398,
          "en": "a get request reaches this page, this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.398,
          "end": 137.25,
          "en": "And the route here, for example, would be slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.25,
          "end": 139.518,
          "en": "expenses slash raw.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 139.518,
          "end": 143.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, whilst in most cases you use loaders in conjunction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 147.15,
          "en": "with components for which they load data, you can also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 147.15,
          "end": 151.29,
          "en": "use loaders standalone to just return some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.29,
          "end": 154.59,
          "en": "and all the actions, by the way, standalone to just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.59,
          "end": 158.024,
          "en": "return some data and perform some action if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.024,
          "end": 163.024,
          "en": "So here, for example, you could return an array of objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 166.921,
          "en": "In this case, some dummy expenses, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.921,
          "end": 169.56,
          "en": "And for that, I'll use the same dummy expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.56,
          "end": 171.78,
          "en": "which I used before already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.78,
          "end": 175.71,
          "en": "The dummy expenses I have here in expenses, jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.71,
          "end": 179.107,
          "en": "for example, I'll copy them, paste them in here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.107,
          "end": 180.951,
          "en": "until we have real expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.951,
          "end": 184.563,
          "en": "and we could return those dummy expenses here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.91,
          "end": 189.18,
          "en": "So that would be a super simple loader that returns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.18,
          "end": 192.633,
          "en": "some data and that does not have a connected component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.62,
          "end": 198.62,
          "en": "If we save this and we visit slash expenses slash raw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.69,
          "end": 202.95,
          "en": "we see that data, and that is how easy it is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.95,
          "end": 205.71,
          "en": "to create a so-called resource route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.71,
          "end": 209.13,
          "en": "A route that does not yield a page, a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.13,
          "end": 210.96,
          "en": "but instead just some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.96,
          "end": 214.74,
          "en": "You simply add a standalone loader without a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.74,
          "end": 217.293,
          "en": "and you return the data that should be returned.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
